<title>JAPAN: Saudi Aramco cuts June propane, butane unchanged.</title>
<headline>Saudi Aramco cuts June propane, butane unchanged.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-06-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Saudi Arabia's state-owned oil firm Saudi Aramco said on Monday it had cut its propane contract price for June by $4 from the previous month to $175 per tonne, but kept the price of butane unchanged at $192.  </p>
<p>The propane price for June is up $5 from a year ago, and that for butane up $12 over the same period.</p>
<p>The Saudi contract price is loosely based on the results of three monthly spot tenders and the company's own assessment of spot market trends.</p>
</text>
